Sval: child processes take names that say what each one does

Activity Monitor listed every website as "SvalCP Isolated Web Content",
which tells a user nothing. The child bundle takes the app's own name, and
each process type a plain label: "Sval Website Renderer" for a site's
process, "Sval Helper (Network)" and the like for the others. The site
itself stays out of the name, because any process of the user's can read
process names and macOS copies them into its diagnostic reports.

